---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ScenicBand from '../../components/ScenicBand.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, pageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'About Horizon Therapy' }];
---

<Layout
  title="About Horizon Therapy | Bozeman, Montana"
  description="Learn about Horizon Therapy, a fictional individual counseling practice for adults in Bozeman, Montana."
  schema={pageSchema([breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, Astro.url.pathname)])}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About Horizon"
    title="A little more room to see where you are—and where you want to go."
    intro="Horizon Therapy is Morgan Hale’s fictional counseling practice in Bozeman, Montana, built around individual therapy for adults navigating change, uncertainty, and difficult seasons."
    crumbs={crumbs}
  />

  <section class="horizon-intro">
    <div class="container intro-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Perspective</p>
        <h2>Sometimes the problem looks different when you can see more of the landscape around it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-copy">
        <p>
          Horizon is designed around the idea that therapy can create distance
          from the immediate noise without disconnecting from real life. A wider
          view can make patterns, choices, losses, and priorities easier to see.
        </p>
        <p>
          That does not mean every problem has a simple answer. It means there
          can be value in knowing the terrain before deciding which direction
          makes sense next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ScenicBand
    image="/images/scenes/meadow-feature.jpg"
    eyebrow="Rooted in Montana"
    title="Space can change what comes into focus."
    position="center 55%"
  />

  <section class="horizon-principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="principle-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What shapes the practice</p>
        <h2>Three ways Horizon thinks about the work.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Start with the terrain you are actually in.</h3>
          <p>
            Therapy can begin with present circumstances, not an idealized
            version of how life is supposed to look or how quickly you should
            be moving through it.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Use perspective before pressure.</h3>
          <p>
            Understanding a pattern, transition, or relationship can create
            better choices than simply demanding that you react differently.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Keep direction connected to what matters.</h3>
          <p>
            Goals are most useful when they reflect your values, relationships,
            responsibilities, and the life you actually want to inhabit.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="horizon-entry">
    <div class="container entry-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Different ways in</p>
        <h2>You can begin with the concern or with curiosity about the process.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="entry-links">
        <a href="/services/">
          <span>Services</span>
          <strong>What are you navigating? →</strong>
        </a>
        <a href="/approaches/">
          <span>Approaches</span>
          <strong>How might the work take shape? →</strong>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="horizon-morgan">
    <div class="container morgan-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Meet the counselor</p>
        <h2>Morgan Hale, LPC</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Morgan’s fictional profile shows how Horizon’s reflective,
          place-oriented identity carries into the clinician story and the
          practical details of individual counseling.
        </p>
        <a href="/about/morgan-hale/">Meet Morgan →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .horizon-intro,
  .horizon-principles,
  .horizon-entry,
  .horizon-morgan {
    padding: clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7rem) 0;
  }

  .intro-grid,
  .entry-grid,
  .morgan-grid {
    display:grid;
    gap:2rem;
  }

  .horizon-intro h2,
  .horizon-principles h2,
  .horizon-entry h2,
  .horizon-morgan h2 {
    font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;
    font-weight:500;
    letter-spacing:-.04em;
  }

  .horizon-intro h2 {
    max-width:15ch;
    font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.8rem);
    line-height:.98;
  }

  .intro-copy {
    max-width:38rem;
    align-self:end;
  }

  .horizon-principles {
    background:#edf0e8;
  }

  .principle-heading {
    max-width:48rem;
    margin-bottom:2.5rem;
  }

  .principle-grid {
    display:grid;
    gap:1rem;
  }

  .principle-grid article {
    padding:1.6rem 0;
    border-top:1px solid #b8c1b5;
  }

  .principle-grid h3 {
    margin-top:.25rem;
    font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;
    font-weight:500;
  }

  .horizon-entry {
    background:#183d3f;
    color:#e8efeb;
  }

  .horizon-entry h2,
  .horizon-entry .eyebrow {
    color:white;
  }

  .entry-links {
    display:grid;
    gap:.75rem;
  }

  .entry-links a {
    display:grid;
    gap:.25rem;
    padding:1.25rem 0;
    border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22);
    color:white;
    text-decoration:none;
  }

  .entry-links span {
    color:#d6ad62;
    font-size:.72rem;
    font-weight:850;
    letter-spacing:.1em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
  }

  .horizon-morgan {
    background:#f6f1e7;
  }

  .horizon-morgan a {
    color:#315a5a;
    font-weight:800;
  }

  @media(min-width:48rem) {
    .intro-grid,
    .entry-grid,
    .morgan-grid {
      grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
      gap:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);
      align-items:start;
    }

    .principle-grid {
      grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
      gap:2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
